Distributed web infrastructure

A user wants to access the website www.foobar.com from their browser.

The user types www.foobar.com. DNS resolves the domain name to the IP address of the load balancer. The user's browser sends an HTTP request to the load balancer. The load balancer distributes the request between two backend servers.

